            "text": "An optimal implementation in Python to compute the sum of Euclidean distances over all ordered pairs within the given resource constraints:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Load the vectors (8000 x 1024, float32)\n    X = np.load(\"vectors.npy\")\n\n    # Compute squared L2 norms for each row: ||x_i||^2\n    sq_norms = np.sum(X * X, axis=1)\n\n    # Compute Gram matrix G = X @ X.T using fast single-precision GEMM\n    G = X @ X.T\n\n    # ||x_i - x_j||^2 = ||x_i||^2 + ||x_j||^2 - 2 * (x_i . x_j)\n    # Perform operations in-place to stay well within the 1024 MiB memory limit\n    G *= -2.0\n    G += sq_norms\n    G += sq_norms[:, None]\n\n    # Guard against negative values from minor floating-point cancellation\n    np.maximum(G, 0.0, out=G)\n    np.sqrt(G, out=G)\n\n    # Explicitly set diagonal to 0.0\n    np.fill_diagonal(G, 0.0)\n\n    # Sum in float64 for numerical precision\n    total = float(G.sum(dtype=np.float64))\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
